Floorp's chrome features extend NoraComponentBase, whose constructor calls init().
A subclass's field initializers run only after that constructor returns, so a field
written as `private x = value;` is set back to `value` right after init() filled it
in. Floorp's own remedy (modal-parent, context-menu) is `declare`, which emits no
initializer. This applies it to the two features where the reset breaks something
in 12.20.1:

  idle-memory-reclaim  the saved setting was replaced by the defaults (off) at every
                       start, so no reclaim ran until the setting changed while the
                       browser was running, and the observers and timer registered
                       at start could never be removed
  tab-sleep-exclusion  saved exclusions were dropped at the first navigation in
                       each new window

Left alone, same pattern: Addons (the Chrome Web Store install state is shared as
undefined; fixing it changes install prompts in ways not tested here), and Pwa,
RebootPanelMenuComponent, HubPanelMenuComponent (no effect).
Found and tested 12/10/2026 against 12.20.1-2 with a rebuilt feature bundle.
Drop a file's part once Floorp fixes that class. Every hunk removes lines, so
`patch` either puts it in the right place or fails.

